New: The local-smoothing GMG solver supports rotated periodicity in 2D
spherical shells with 90- and 180-degree opening angles. The geometry model
supplies velocity constraints through the public deal.II level-periodicity
API and MGConstrainedDoFs::add_user_constraints(). Adaptive refinement keeps
periodic partners on matching levels; meshes with existing periodic hanging
nodes are still rejected. This feature requires the API introduced by deal.II
PR #20212, whose availability is checked at configuration time. Older deal.II
versions can still be used for the existing solver paths. Solver defaults
are unchanged: select block GMG and local smoothing explicitly.
<br>
